<title>RUSSIA: Russian MinFins little changed, seen rising.</title>
<headline>Russian MinFins little changed, seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>MinFin bonds were almost unchanged in lethargic trading on Monday due to the U.S. President's Day holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>    tranche		 Feb 17		  Feb 14</p>
<p>    1999 maturity (3)   86.80-87.10	   86.88-87.25</p>
<p>    2003 maturity (4)   63.70-64.00	   63.75-64.00</p>
<p>    2008 maturity (5)   44.80-45.10	   44.88-45.00</p>
<p>    2006 maturity (6)   50.80-51.10	   50.75-51.13</p>
<p>    2011 maturity (7)   37.80-38.10	   37.88-38.38</p>
<p>&quot;The market is dead, London closed at about noon, and there were two or three deals between Russian banks,&quot; said Bank Imperial chief dealer Alexei Denisov.</p>
<p>Denisov forecast a rising market in the next few days.</p>
<p>&quot;The market has potential due to the spread to the U.S. paper,&quot; he said. &quot;The way up is more realistic than the way down.&quot;</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
